<title>CHINA: TYSAN YEAR NET PROFIT RISES 21 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>TYSAN YEAR NET PROFIT RISES 21 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(In million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   24.2	 vs 18.8 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    5.2	  vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  39.56 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    126.10     vs 85</p>
<p>    Turnover		     735.96     vs 880.70</p>
<p>    Company name		 Tysan Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 16-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 18</p>
<p>NOTE - Tysan is engaged in foundation piling, property development and machinery hiring.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of subsidiaries.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings have been adjusted to take into account the effect of a bonus issue.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is 7.8 cents (including interim dividend of 2.6 cents) vs seven cents. ($1 = HK$7.8)</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
